e of Sergipe, in northeastern Brazil, about 350 km (217 mi) north of Salvador. According to the 2020 estimate, the city has 664,908 inhabitants, which represents approximately 33% of the state population. Adding to the populations of the municipalities forming the Metropolitan area: Barra dos Coqueiros, Nossa Senhora do Socorro and São Cristóvão. Its Metropolitan Cathedral Nossa Senhora da Conceiçao, dedicated to Our Lady of Immaculate Conception, is the archiepiscopal see of the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Aracaju.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Ponte_do_Imperador_Aracaju.jpg/330px-Ponte_do_Imperador_Aracaju.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aracaju"},"twins":[],"climate":{"temp":[27.2,27.4,27.7,27.5,26.7,25.8,25,24.7,25.2,26,26.5,27],"rain":[56,58,74,116,191,158,144,89,58,47,27,24],"cloud":[61,63,56,52,53,56,56,52,44,45,46,55]}}